  "scope_id": "COPRIME-CLASS2-20261026-001",
  "title": "A dichotomy for Heisenberg-by-cyclic groups with bounded homology, and a counterexample to Rowell's conjecture",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold and knot groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "For Heisenberg groups over odd prime fields with a coprime cyclic action, counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology is #P-hard exactly when the action's three characters are nontrivial (else polynomial), already on knot surgeries and knot groups, because Borromean moves steer a three-way eigen-triple form into a Potts gadget. Hence Rowell's 2009 conjecture of polynomial exact counting on link groups for solvable targets fails, also for S4, unless #P functions are polynomial-time computable.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
